comment:
@mkbhd have you noticed any difference in the glass quality from previous generations, to the 15?  I just upgraded from an iPhone XS that I've had since ~2019.  The screen does show some signs of age/wear and tear, but the new 15 Pro I just bought already has a fine scratch on the screen that's far more noticeable than anything on the XS it replaced.  I'm religious about ensuring my phone goes in a pocket by itself to prevent this type of damage, and it's a little disheartening to see that it's scraped already.

Just wondering if you'd be willing to share your experience now that it's a couple of months down the road.

Regardless, great video and I appreciate your insights into the phone I just bought!

Uri Avnery admittedly said on establishment of I$rael;
“No one asked the Arab Palestinians whether to accept or reject anything. If they had been asked, they would
probably have rejected partition, since—in their view—it gave a large part of their historical homeland to foreigners. The governments of the Arab states rejected partition, but they certainly did not represent the Palestinian Arabs, who were at the time still under British rule (as were we).”
